  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 605</b></color></size>\n<b>The rupiya of Sher Shah Suri</b>\n<size=74%>1540\u20131545\n<i>Silver, about 11.5 g</i>\nVarious museum collections</size>\n<size=70%><line-height=110%>\nSher Shah Suri, who briefly drove the Mughal emperor Humayun out of India, introduced a standard silver coin called the rupiya. The Mughals and later the British kept it, and its name lives on in the rupee used in India and several neighbouring countries.</size>"
