  m_text: '<size=70%><color=#9A6A2E><b>AUDIO 610</b></color></size>

    <b>Aryabhata, India''s first satellite (replica)</b>

    <size=74%>Launched 19 April 1975

    <i>Replica; the original was a 26-sided polyhedron about 1.4 m across, weighing 360 kg</i>

    Replica made for this museum</size>

    <size=70%><line-height=110%>

    Named after the 5th-century mathematician and astronomer, India''s first satellite was designed and built by ISRO in Bengaluru and launched by a Soviet rocket on 19 April 1975. Its faces were covered with solar cells. It carried experiments in X-ray astronomy and solar physics.</size>

    <size=50%><color=#8A8A8A>Replica made for this museum</color></size>'
